00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:23,000
the earliest livestock domesticated in southwest Asia. Cattle were domesticated from orox. These animals initially

130
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:32,000
supplied meat, hides, bone and other resources. Then humans discovered secondary products. Milk, wool,

131
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:38,000
traction. Instead of killing an animal once, you could keep extracting value.

132
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Archaeologists can detect ancient dairying partly through lipid residues preserved in pottery. Milk fats leave chemical signatures that can sometimes be distinguished from carcass fats.

133
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:58,000
These residues show dairying existed in parts of Southwest Asia and Europe thousands of years ago, reaching back into the Neolithic.

134
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Once communities developed dairy economies, selection intensified, animals that produced more milk became

135
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:12,000
