160
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:28,000
dairy becomes even more expensive. If making one small wheel requires milking a crowd of dogs, the wheel should come with financing options. Novelty products

161
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:40,000
prove the point. Cow cheese became ordinary because cow milk became abundant. There is another reason pigs were poorly positioned for dairying. Pig reproduction prioritizes many offspring.

162
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:47,000
A cow usually produces one calf at a time. A goat often produces one to a few kids. A sa can produce a large litter.

163
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Her memory system distributes milk among many mouths simultaneously.

164
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:58,000
The many small teeth are part of that reproductive strategy. Dogs also produce litters. Their memory anatomy follows

165
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:06,000
the same broad problem. Cows put enormous milk output through four convenient exits. Pigs and dogs distribute it across a biological

166
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:14,000
cafeteria. Humans chose the species with easier plumbing. Could people somewhere in history have tasted pig or dog milk?

167
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:20,000
Almost certainly. Humans are curious, hungry, and repeatedly willing to put questionable substances in their mouths.

168
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:30,000
There are scattered historical anecdotes and novelty experiments involving unusual milks. But occasional consumption is not a dairy tradition. A

169
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:33,000
